<div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 24px;">
  <img src="https://www.qbcc.qld.gov.au/sites/default/files/QBCC_logo.png" alt="QBCC" style="height: 60px; margin-bottom: 12px;">
  <h1 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: bold; margin: 0;">CONSUMER BUILDING GUIDE</h1>
  <p style="font-size: 11px; margin: 8px 0 0 0;">Your Guide to Building in Queensland</p>
</div>

<p style="font-size: 10px; background: #e3f2fd; padding: 12px; border-left: 4px solid #2196f3; margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <strong>IMPORTANT:</strong> This guide contains essential information about your rights and responsibilities
  when building a new home in Queensland. Please read it carefully before signing your building contract.
</p>

<h2 style="font-size: 14px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 6px 8px; margin: 16px 0 8px 0;">1. BEFORE YOU SIGN</h2>

<h3 style="font-size: 11px; font-weight: bold; margin: 12px 0 8px 0;">Check the Contractor's Licence</h3>
<p style="font-size: 10px; margin: 0 0 8px 0;">
  Before signing any contract, verify that your builder holds a current QBCC licence. You can check
  licence details at <strong>www.qbcc.qld.gov.au</strong> or call <strong>139 333</strong>.
</p>

<table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 12px;">
  <tr>
    <td style="width: 30%; background: #f0f0f0; padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000; font-size: 10px;">Your Contractor:</td>
    <td style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000; font-size: 10px;"><%= @company[:name] %></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="background: #f0f0f0; padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000; font-size: 10px;">QBCC Licence Number:</td>
    <td style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000; font-size: 10px;"><%= @company[:qbcc_license] %></td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h3 style="font-size: 11px; font-weight: bold; margin: 12px 0 8px 0;">Get Everything in Writing</h3>
<p style="font-size: 10px; margin: 0 0 8px 0;">
  Ensure all agreements, promises, and specifications are included in your written contract. Verbal
  agreements may be difficult to enforce. Your contract should include:
</p>
<ul style="font-size: 10px; margin: 0 0 8px 16px; padding: 0;">
  <li>Detailed plans and specifications</li>
  <li>The total contract price (including GST)</li>
  <li>A progress payment schedule</li>
  <li>Start and completion dates</li>
  <li>Any special conditions or inclusions</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size: 14px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 6px 8px; margin: 16px 0 8px 0;">2. YOUR COOLING-OFF PERIOD</h2>

<div style="background: #fff3cd; border: 2px solid #ffc107; padding: 12px; margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 10px;">
  <strong>5 BUSINESS DAYS</strong><br>
  After signing a domestic building contract, you have <strong>5 business days</strong> to change your mind.
  During this period, you can terminate the contract by giving written notice to the contractor.
</div>

<p style="font-size: 10px; margin: 0 0 8px 0;">
  If you terminate during the cooling-off period:
</p>
<ul style="font-size: 10px; margin: 0 0 8px 16px; padding: 0;">
  <li>You may be required to pay for reasonable expenses the contractor has already incurred</li>
  <li>These may include costs for plans, engineering, or council applications</li>
  <li>The contractor must provide an itemised account of these costs</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size: 14px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 6px 8px; margin: 16px 0 8px 0;">3. DEPOSITS AND PROGRESS PAYMENTS</h2>

<h3 style="font-size: 11px; font-weight: bold; margin: 12px 0 8px 0;">Maximum Deposit</h3>
<p style="font-size: 10px; margin: 0 0 8px 0;">
  The maximum deposit a contractor can request is:
</p>
<ul style="font-size: 10px; margin: 0 0 8px 16px; padding: 0;">
  <li><strong>5%</strong> of the contract price for contracts over $20,000, OR</li>
  <li><strong>$1,000</strong> for contracts between $3,300 and $20,000</li>
</ul>

<h3 style="font-size: 11px; font-weight: bold; margin: 12px 0 8px 0;">Progress Payments</h3>
<p style="font-size: 10px; margin: 0 0 8px 0;">
  For contracts over $20,000, the contractor can only claim progress payments when specific stages
  are completed. Standard stages include:
</p>

<table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 10px;">
  <tr style="background: #f0f0f0;">
    <th style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000; text-align: left;">Stage</th>
    <th style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000; text-align: left;">Description</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000;">Base Stage</td>
    <td style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000;">Slab or stumps laid</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000;">Frame Stage</td>
    <td style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000;">Roof covering complete, wall frames fixed</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000;">Enclosed Stage</td>
    <td style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000;">External wall cladding and windows fitted</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000;">Fixing Stage</td>
    <td style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000;">Internal linings, doors, trims installed</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000;">Practical Completion</td>
    <td style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000;">Building complete and ready for occupation</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="font-size: 14px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 6px 8px; margin: 16px 0 8px 0;">4. VARIATIONS TO THE CONTRACT</h2>

<p style="font-size: 10px; margin: 0 0 8px 0;">
  Any changes to the original contract must be agreed in writing. A variation should include:
</p>
<ul style="font-size: 10px; margin: 0 0 8px 16px; padding: 0;">
  <li>A clear description of the changed work</li>
  <li>The cost of the variation (additions or credits)</li>
  <li>Any impact on the completion date</li>
  <li>Signatures from both parties</li>
</ul>

<div style="background: #ffebee; border-left: 4px solid #f44336; padding: 8px 12px; margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-size: 10px;">
  <strong>Warning:</strong> Never authorise variations verbally. Always get variations in writing before
  work commences.
</div>

<h2 style="font-size: 14px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 6px 8px; margin: 16px 0 8px 0;">5. STATUTORY WARRANTIES</h2>

<p style="font-size: 10px; margin: 0 0 8px 0;">
  Under the <em>Queensland Building and Construction Commission Act 1991</em>, all domestic building
  work comes with statutory warranties:
</p>

<table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 10px; margin-bottom: 12px;">
  <tr style="background: #f0f0f0;">
    <th style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000; text-align: left;">Defect Type</th>
    <th style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000; text-align: left;">Warranty Period</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000;">Non-structural defects</td>
    <td style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000;">6 months from completion</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000;">Structural defects</td>
    <td style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000;">6 years and 6 months from completion</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000;">Subsidence or settlement</td>
    <td style="padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px solid #000;">6 years and 6 months from completion</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="font-size: 14px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 6px 8px; margin: 16px 0 8px 0;">6. QBCC HOME WARRANTY INSURANCE</h2>

<p style="font-size: 10px; margin: 0 0 8px 0;">
  For contracts valued at $3,300 or more (including GST), the QBCC provides automatic insurance
  protection. This covers you if:
</p>
<ul style="font-size: 10px; margin: 0 0 8px 16px; padding: 0;">
  <li>The contractor dies, disappears, or becomes insolvent</li>
  <li>The contractor fails to complete work or fix defects</li>
  <li>There are defects in the work during the warranty period</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size: 14px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 6px 8px; margin: 16px 0 8px 0;">7. RESOLVING DISPUTES</h2>

<p style="font-size: 10px; margin: 0 0 8px 0;">
  If you have concerns during your build:
</p>
<ol style="font-size: 10px; margin: 0 0 8px 16px; padding: 0;">
  <li>First, try to resolve the issue directly with your contractor in writing</li>
  <li>If unresolved, contact the QBCC for advice or to lodge a complaint</li>
  <li>The QBCC can investigate complaints and take action if needed</li>
</ol>

<div style="background: #e8f5e9; border: 1px solid #4caf50; padding: 12px; margin: 16px 0; font-size: 10px;">
  <strong>Need Help?</strong><br>
  Contact the Queensland Building and Construction Commission:<br>
  <strong>Phone:</strong> 139 333<br>
  <strong>Website:</strong> www.qbcc.qld.gov.au
</div>

<h2 style="font-size: 14px; background: #000; color: #fff; padding: 6px 8px; margin: 16px 0 8px 0;">8. ACKNOWLEDGEMENT</h2>

<p style="font-size: 10px; margin: 0 0 16px 0;">
  I/We acknowledge that I/we have received, read, and understood this Consumer Building Guide
  before signing the building contract.
</p>

